How does the model know when to stop?

The key idea is that generation has a stopping condition.

At each generation step, the model predicts a probability distribution over possible next tokens:

"I am an AI" + ?
                 ↓
        probability distribution
                 ↓
        "agent"   42%
        "model"   18%
        "system"  7%
        ...
        <EOS>     0.3%

Instead, the model generates tokens until the generation process encounters a condition that tells the runtime to stop.
